Time Complexity

At each row:

You have n - 1 choices (every column except the current one).

There are n rows, so the recursion tree has approximately:

Level 0: n starting columns
Level 1: n - 1 choices
Level 2: n - 1 choices
...
Level n - 1

So the total time is:

O(n⋅(n−1)
n−1
)
	​


This is exponential.

People often simplify it as:

O(n
n
)
	​


Time Complexity: O(n × (n−1)^(n−1)) (commonly written as O(n^n))
Space Complexity: O(n)

class Solution {
public:
    int solve(int row, int col, vector<vector<int>>& grid)
    {
        int n = grid.size();

        if (row == n - 1)
            return grid[row][col];

        int mini = INT_MAX;

        for (int k = 0; k < n; k++)
        {
            if (k != col)
            {
                mini = min(mini, solve(row + 1, k, grid));
            }
        }

        return grid[row][col] + mini;
    }

    int minFallingPathSum(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {
        int n = grid.size();

        int ans = INT_MAX;

        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
        {
            ans = min(ans, solve(0, j, grid));
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

